  "decision_conditions": [
    "The roof area of the development hereby approved shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or sitting out area at any time.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and supporting documents and thereafter maintained as such for the lifetime of the development: - drawing number Location Site Map, P.1 P.2; P.3; P.4; P.5; P.6; P.7; P.8 (11 May 2022) and E.1; E.2; E.3; E.4; E.5 &amp;amp; E,6 (16 June 2021) - documents entitled Planning Statement dated May 2024, Design and Access Statement/Planning Statement dated July 2024, Crime Prevention/Safer Places Report.&amp;nbsp;",
    "The materials to be used for the external surfaces of the development/extension hereby permitted shall match those of the existing building and shall thereafter be retained as such for the lifetime of the development.",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;Prior to commencement of any development on the site, a specification for a highway site condition survey to assess the condition of the public highway before and after construction works shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The condition survey shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved timescales contained within the approved specification and it shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before any part of the development is occupied. Any damage to the highway incurred as a result of the construction works will be reinstated by the Council and funded by the developer, in accordance with the timescales and details agreed as part of the survey.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;Prior to commencement of the development, notwithstanding site investigation and clearance works, full details relating to the proposed bicycle parking shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include the proposed design and materials of the cycle stores. The development shall be carried out fully in accordance with the approved details prior to occupation of the development and shall be thereafter maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;font face=&quot;Calibri, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px;&quot;&gt;Prior to occupation, the development shall achieve a Certificate of Compliance to the relevant Secure by Design Guide(s) or alternatively achieve Crime Prevention Standards submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority in conjunction with the Metropolitan Police.&amp;nbsp; The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and thereafter shall be fully retained and maintained as such for the lifetime of the development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;",
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than the expiration of three years from the date of this permission."
  ],
